factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The reel_script and slides say the 14 books were 'removed' and sent to the district library, but the article only says they were packed up and sent to the Salem district central library; calling the removal itself a fact is roughly consistent, so no clear error there.
  The reel_script, slides and caption say the books were 'given' by the publisher in January 2025, but the article says the books were found in the library as delivered from the publisher in January 2025, so the timing is consistent; however, the article does not state why the books were removed beyond the controversy, and the draft presents the controversy as the direct cause ('ஏன் அகற்றம்?'), which the article does not explicitly state.
  The article says the Coimbatore library had fake books that prompted a review of controversial books in all libraries; the draft says 'போலி நூல்கள் புகார்' (complaint of fake books), which is a reasonable paraphrase, but the slide claims 'ஏன் அகற்றம்' (why removed) as an established cause, which the article does not confirm.
  The caption and reel_script say the library is 'மாவட்ட கிளை நூலகம்' (district branch library) and the headline says 'ஆத்தூர் கிளை நூலகம்'; the article calls it both 'ஆத்தூர் கிளை நூலகம்' and 'மாவட்ட கிளை நூலகம்', so this is consistent.
  The reel_script states the books are 'சர்ச்சைக்குரிய' (controversial) without the article clearly stating that the 14 books themselves were labelled controversial; the article only says the books from this publisher were found in the library after the Coimbatore complaint.
